              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रटना — raṭnā — \"to learn by rote, to cram\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अगर तुम केवल रटोगे तो कुछ नहीं समझोगे। agar tum keval raṭoge to kuch nahīṃ samjhoge. If you only learn by rote, you won't understand anything."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने पूरा पाठ रटा, usne pūrā pāṭh raṭā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रटना (raṭnā) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit raṭati, \"cries, yells\" (CDIAL 10590). Hindi uses the sense of saying over and over."
            }
          ]
        },
